  "term": "progressive bulbar palsy",
  "definition": "Progressive bulbar palsy is a worsening motor neuron disorder that affects muscles controlled by cranial nerves in the lower brainstem. It commonly causes problems with chewing, swallowing, and speech, along with weakness in the face and tongue.",
